                        "form_id": "6c6d7e96-06db-48f2-90b4-3f5ed7fc01f4",
                        "entry_id": "8dcb2228-f18a-38b0-a1e4-1381f533c6d4",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "tabards"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a18b39d2-3f2f-3883-8636-cdeb2019e8b2",
                        "entry_id": "8dcb2228-f18a-38b0-a1e4-1381f533c6d4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A silk banner attached to a bugle or trumpet."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e9c63ff0-0a55-36a4-be99-2026003ce845",
                        "entry_id": "8dcb2228-f18a-38b0-a1e4-1381f533c6d4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A sleeveless jerkin or loose overgarment."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8b339e2b-2350-445d-8d38-ef5137e11323",
                                "sense_id": "e9c63ff0-0a55-36a4-be99-2026003ce845",
                                "text": "The long rows of wheat-shocks marched like soldiers in worn yellow tabards."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bb00a8d2-3d1a-4882-952c-d6d7b077481d",
                                "sense_id": "e9c63ff0-0a55-36a4-be99-2026003ce845",
                                "text": "‘I still cannot believe I actually did that!’ Maureen told me, recalling that time her and the Nanas turned up at former prime minister David Cameron's house in Oxfordshire on a tank Vivienne Westwood lent them, wearing tabards that said ‘The Oven Gloves Are Coming Off’."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "54b9eeef-8d31-4319-85f1-2c49d840129b",
                                "sense_id": "e9c63ff0-0a55-36a4-be99-2026003ce845",
                                "text": "This is the point at which someone usually suggests riders wear a numbered, hi-vis tabard."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0f5c7ff5-fbcb-3641-a6e3-e1757622d865",
                        "entry_id": "8dcb2228-f18a-38b0-a1e4-1381f533c6d4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A sleeveless garment made of coarse cloth formerly worn outdoors by the common people."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a84894bb-3413-382f-9b2e-7dfe1951898a",
                        "entry_id": "8dcb2228-f18a-38b0-a1e4-1381f533c6d4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A cape or tunic worn by a knight, emblazoned with the coat of arms of his king or queen on the front."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "422f3327-e191-4755-92ac-67c1ca3b2e35",
                                "sense_id": "a84894bb-3413-382f-9b2e-7dfe1951898a",
                                "text": "And thereupon, behold, a knight on a black horse appeared, clothed in jet-black velvet, and with a tabard of black linen about him."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c270ee02-a379-31ff-bb40-af0d2b72da4b",
                        "entry_id": "8dcb2228-f18a-38b0-a1e4-1381f533c6d4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A similar garment officially worn by a herald and emblazoned with his sovereign's coat of arms."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ac8d5601-35be-4b4f-a525-1de53c0f3fbe",
                                "sense_id": "c270ee02-a379-31ff-bb40-af0d2b72da4b",
                                "text": "The heralds in their tabards were marvellous to behold, and a nod from Rouge Croix gave me the keenest gratification."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0128f441-7eb8-478d-a4bd-37164b3cc70a",
                                "sense_id": "c270ee02-a379-31ff-bb40-af0d2b72da4b",
                                "text": "Along the narrow winding path between the great oak trees there rode a dark sallow man in a scarlet tabard who blew so loudly upon a silver trumpet that they heard the clanging call long before they set eyes on him."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b5b6b5e9-597a-4f00-a1b8-ff8c6b3828a2",
                        "source_entry_id": "8dcb2228-f18a-38b0-a1e4-1381f533c6d4",
                        "source_sense_description": "sleeveless jerkin",
                        "target_lang_word": "tabard",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tabard",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "71434ebe-cf40-3a73-89d6-66bc2c499d41",
                                        "entry_id": "66661d97-ad5f-3f33-b8d9-e18425fb3e24",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Vêtement du dessus médiéval fait d'une courte veste aux manches en forme d'ailerons, enfilé par-dessus l'armure."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c30831a7-0183-4cb3-b99d-905c6b88dc9a",
                                                "sense_id": "71434ebe-cf40-3a73-89d6-66bc2c499d41",
                                                "text": "Mais ce qui donne à la procession un caractère tout particulier, c’est le héraut d’armes de la cité de Londres, vêtu comme au moyen âge, avec un tabard historié du blason d’Angleterre ; ce sont des chevaliers couverts de pied en cap d’armures d’or et d’acier, suivis de leurs pages portant la lance et l’écu, qui marchent isolés, de distance en distance, entre les divers pelotons."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "94a0c8f3-c2d1-3bc7-bd46-70c4c26f6bde",
                                        "entry_id": "66661d97-ad5f-3f33-b8d9-e18425fb3e24",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Dalmatique du héraut. Il est généralement brodé aux armoiries de l’office ou employeur du héraut. Le vêtement présente quatre surfaces (face, dos et sur chacun des bras) sur lesquelles les armoiries sont reproduites, permettant à quiconque de les voir quelle que soit sa position par rapport au héraut."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
